{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggCuSokSYLGS7PNCFXiA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The least-squares fit gives Dq ≈ 1085 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹, with C ≈ 3707 cm⁻¹ from C/B = 4.5. The fit reproduces the three bands only to within about 280 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Method.** I fitted the three bands with the `ts_fit_spectrum` tool, using the high-spin d⁸ spin-allowed manifold. That manifold doesn't depend on C. The tool warned that C is assumed rather than constrained by these bands, and I had passed it C = 3990. Re-fitting with C = 3707 would not change Dq or B.\n\n**Fit results.**\n\n| Band | Assignment | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ν₁ | ³A₂ → ³T₂ | 10 600 | 10 846 |\n| ν₂ | ³A₂ → ³T₁(F) | 17 500 | 17 216 |\n| ν₃ | ³A₂ → ³T₁(P) | 27 600 | 27 680 |\n\n- The residuals are +246, −284 and +80 cm⁻¹, so the fit is good but not exact.\n- Because ν₁ = 10Dq, the lowest band alone would give Dq = 1060 cm⁻¹. The global fit moves Dq slightly to 1085 cm⁻¹ to compromise with the two upper bands.\n\n**Hand check (not reliable).** I tried solving the ³T₁ matrix by hand with Dq = 1060 cm⁻¹. It gave B ≈ 887 cm⁻¹, but the predicted ν₂ and ν₃ were about 16 200 and 28 900 cm⁻¹, which is poor. I suspect an error in the matrix elements I used, so I rely on the tool result instead.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1085, \"B\": 824, \"C\": 3707, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Least-squares fit of the three spin-allowed d8 bands (³T₂, ³T₁, ³T₁(2)) gives Dq≈1085 and B≈824 cm⁻¹, with C=4.5B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2624,"cache_read_input_tokens":8036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pare